#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:0
msgid ""
"Resolve common snap and snapd issues with network access, daemon "
"connectivity, slow downloads, missing binaries, home directories, and "
"initialisation errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:8
msgid "Fix common issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:10
msgid ""
"Snaps run on, and are built for, a diverse and constantly evolving set of "
"{ref}`operating systems <tutorials-install-the-daemon-index>` and [embedded "
"devices](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/core/reference/testing-platforms/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:12
msgid ""
"The vast majority of our users and developers experience very few issues, "
"but any technology this complex and diverse will likely encounter some "
"issues and incompatibilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:14
msgid ""
"This page attempts to guide users to either an appropriate solution to their "
"issues, or the correct forum/thread where they can get help."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:16
msgid "Network access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:18
msgid ""
"The snap daemon (snapd) requires network access to install, update, build "
"and publish snaps. Local network and port configurations can affect their "
"access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:20
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Network requirements <reference-administration-network-"
"requirements>` for which hosts and ports are required to ensure consistent "
"communication."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:22
msgid "Cannot communicate with the server / connection refused"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:24
msgid ""
"To perform most actions, the snap client needs to communicate with the snap "
"daemon. If this isn't possible, the snap command fails and outputs a "
"connection refused error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:26
msgid ""
"There are various causes for this error.  Try the following steps, and if "
"the problem persists, see the next section on generating and sharing "
"debugging details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:28
msgid "Restart snapd:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:30
msgid "sudo systemctl restart snapd snapd.socket\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:34
msgid "Reload systemd's daemon state:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:36
msgid "sudo systemctl daemon-reload\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:40
msgid "Reboot the machine:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:42
msgid "sudo reboot\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:46
msgid ""
"See [cannot communicate with server connection refused ](https://"
"forum.snapcraft.io/t/snap-d-error-cannot-communicate-with-server-connection-"
"refused/6093) for discussions on this issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:48
msgid "Slow snap downloads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:50
msgid ""
"When a snap is installed, it's downloaded and authenticated against one or "
"more servers attached to the [Snap Store](https://snapcraft.io/store) (or a "
"local proxy). If a server is unavailable, or suffering bandwidth issues, "
"installation progress will be slow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:52
msgid ""
"You can check on the operational status of the servers attached to the Snap "
"Store from the Snap Store status page: [https://status.snapcraft.io/]"
"(https://status.snapcraft.io/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:54
msgid ""
"![Snap Store status](https://assets.ubuntu.com/v1/dd75734c-image+%282%29.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:54
msgid "Snap Store status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:56
msgid ""
"The Snap Store Status page also includes a status history for the servers "
"over the last week and an incident history."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:58
msgid ""
"![Snap Store incident report](https://assets.ubuntu.com/v1/5af8a398-"
"image.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:58
msgid "Snap Store incident report"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:60
msgid ""
"See [Extremely slow snap downloads](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/extremely-"
"slow-snap-downloads/4668/38) for further discussions on snap download speeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:62
msgid "Missing binaries / command not found"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:64
msgid ""
"When the snap daemon is installed, its executable components are added to "
"the system path ($PATH). If this doesn't happen correctly, a warning is "
"issued stating that snapd cannot be found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:66
msgid ""
"The first thing to do is check installation instructions for the specific "
"operating system. See {ref}`Installing snapd <tutorials-install-the-daemon-"
"index>` for further details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:68
msgid ""
"Linux distributions differ, but most will need a restart after snapd has "
"been installed to refresh paths and system security profiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:70
msgid ""
"Executables from installed snaps can usually be found in `/snap/bin/`, and "
"this should also be in your path. You can check this by typing `echo $PATH | "
"grep \"snap/bin\"` on the command line, or by using the _which_ command to "
"see where the executable binary:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:72
msgid ""
"$ which spotify\n"
"/snap/bin/spotify\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:77
msgid ""
"If an executable isn't in your path, try using the `snap run` command, such "
"as `snap run spotify`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:79
msgid ""
"You can also manually add `/snap/bin` to your system $PATH. This is "
"typically accomplished by adding a line similar to the following in your "
"shell environment's configuration file (such as `~/.bashrc` or `~/.zshrc`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:81
msgid "export PATH=\"/snap/bin:$PATH\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:85
msgid "You will need to restart your shell for the changes to take effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:87
msgid "Home directories outside of /home"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:89
msgid ""
"The snap daemon (snapd) requires a user’s home directory ($HOME) to be "
"located under  `/home`  on the local filesystem. This requirement cannot "
"currently be changed. However, it is possible to  *bind mount*  an "
"alternative $HOME location to  `/home`  to allow other locations to be found "
"by snapd. This process is outlined below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:91
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Home directories outside of ‘/home’ <interfaces-home-outside-"
"home>` for further details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:93
msgid "Domain served /home directories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:95
msgid ""
"Domain-mounted home directories beneath `/home/<DOMAIN-NAME>` may require "
"extra AppArmor permissions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:97
msgid ""
"These can be granted by running `sudo dpkg-reconfigure apparmor` and "
"entering `/home/<DOMAIN-NAME>/`, replacing <DOMAIN-NAME> with your domain, "
"as an additional home directory location at the prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:97
msgid "<DOMAIN-NAME>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:99
msgid "chmod errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:101
msgid ""
"There is a known [issue](https://bugs.launchpad.net/snapd/+bug/1914786) "
"affecting some Debian 10 users, alongside some other Linux distributions "
"users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:103
msgid ""
"Snaps that depend on a _browser-sandbox_, such as Teams and Chromium, may "
"inadvertently exit without an error, although logs should reveal an "
"_incorrect chmod (4755)_ error caused by the following system call:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:105
msgid ""
"`clone(child_stack=0x7ffc0ea30060, flags=CLONE_NEWUSER|SIGCHLD) = -1 EPERM "
"(Operation not permitted)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:107
msgid ""
"As a temporary solution, the issues can be bypassed with the following "
"command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:109
msgid "sudo sysctl kernel.unprivileged_userns_clone=1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:112
msgid "Too early for operation errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:114
msgid ""
"After installing the snap daemon, _snapd_, it can take a short amount of "
"time to initialise its environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:116
msgid ""
"During this initialisation period, if certain instructions are attempted "
"either from the `snap` command or the {ref}`REST API <reference-development-"
"snapd-rest-api>`, the following error may be generated:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:118
msgid ""
"`error: too early for operation, device not yet seeded or device model not "
"acknowledged`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:120
msgid ""
"The solution to errors like these is simply to wait a short while before "
"attempting the same instruction again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:122
msgid "Generate debug info"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:124
msgid ""
"One of the best ways to solve an issue is to understand when and where the "
"error is encountered, and there are several levels of output that can be "
"generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:126
msgid ""
"The `snap changes` and `snap tasks <change-id>` commands, for example, "
"output details about what changed during the last refresh:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:128
msgid ""
"$ snap changes\n"
"ID    Status  Spawn                   Ready                   Summary\n"
"2052  Done    today at 09:34 BST      today at 09:35 BST      Auto-refresh 7 "
"snaps\n"
"2053  Done    today at 15:16 BST      today at 15:17 BST      Refresh snaps "
"\"gnome-calculator\", \"flock-chat\", \"gnome-characters\", \"gnome-system-"
"monitor\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:135
msgid ""
"The snap daemon documents its operations to the system log. This can be "
"retrieved and viewed with the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:137
msgid "sudo journalctl --no-pager -u snapd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:141
msgid "The `snap debug` command can be used to probe the state of the daemon:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:143
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap debug state /var/lib/snapd/state.json\n"
"ID    Status  Spawn                   Ready                   "
"Label                         Summary\n"
"2955  Done    yesterday at 13:53 BST  yesterday at 13:53 BST  hotplug-remove-"
"serial-port    Remove hotplug connections and slots of device /dev/ttyACM0 "
"(Keyboardio Model…; serial: Ckbio01E) with interface \"serial-port\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/fix-common-issues.md:149
msgid ""
"Don't forget to include the output from `sudo snap version` if you wish to "
"share your output to get further help on the forum."
msgstr ""
